From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 23:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] media: cedrus: refuse buffers that would leave too little
 memory

With __GFP_RETRY_MAYFAIL, a CAPTURE pool that is too large for the
board no longer invokes the OOM killer, but the allocation fails only
once the page allocator can reclaim nothing more. Each 111 MB buffer of
a 6144x3456 10-bit H.265 stream first pushes out the page cache, the
program text of every process and, to swap, their anonymous memory. On
a 1 GB board the system then stalls for long enough that the hardware
watchdog resets it, about 30 seconds into the stream, before the
allocation fails.

Check in queue_setup that the requested buffers fit in the memory the
kernel reports as available (si_mem_available(), which already leaves
out the reclaim watermarks) with a sixteenth of the total memory left
over, and fail VIDIOC_REQBUFS/VIDIOC_CREATE_BUFS with -ENOMEM
otherwise. Only MMAP buffers are counted: imported dma-bufs
are not allocated here. __GFP_RETRY_MAYFAIL stays as the backstop for
memory taken by others between the check and the allocation.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_video.c
+++ b/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_video.c
@@ -13,6 +13,7 @@
  * Marek Szyprowski, <m.szyprowski@samsung.com>
  */
 
+#include <linux/mm.h>
 #include <linux/pm_runtime.h>
 
 #include <media/videobuf2-dma-contig.h>
@@ -970,6 +971,35 @@
 	.vidioc_unsubscribe_event	= v4l2_event_unsubscribe,
 };
 
+/*
+ * Buffers are allocated with __GFP_RETRY_MAYFAIL, which fails only once
+ * nothing more can be reclaimed. A pool that takes the memory down to that
+ * point leaves the rest of the system thrashing long before the last
+ * allocation fails (on a 1 GB board, long enough for the watchdog to reset
+ * it), so refuse buffers that would leave less than a sixteenth of the
+ * memory available.
+ */
+static int cedrus_buffers_fit(struct cedrus_ctx *ctx, struct vb2_queue *vq,
+			      unsigned int count, unsigned int size)
+{
+	unsigned long pages = (unsigned long)count * PFN_UP(size);
+	unsigned long reserve = totalram_pages() / 16;
+	long available;
+
+	if (vq->memory != VB2_MEMORY_MMAP)
+		return 0;
+
+	available = si_mem_available();
+	if (available > 0 && pages + reserve <= (unsigned long)available)
+		return 0;
+
+	dev_dbg(ctx->dev->dev,
+		"%u buffers of %u bytes do not fit (%ld kB available)\n",
+		count, size, available << (PAGE_SHIFT - 10));
+
+	return -ENOMEM;
+}
+
 static int cedrus_queue_setup(struct vb2_queue *vq, unsigned int *nbufs,
 			      unsigned int *nplanes, unsigned int sizes[],
 			      struct device *alloc_devs[])
@@ -990,7 +1020,7 @@
 		*nplanes = 1;
 	}
 
-	return 0;
+	return cedrus_buffers_fit(ctx, vq, *nbufs, sizes[0]);
 }
 
 static void cedrus_queue_cleanup(struct vb2_queue *vq, u32 state)
-- 
